mportant role after all of this  foreshadowing I simply can't see any  other possibility the fact that Arthur  will return means that this fight  between meliodas and the demon king  zelgius won't be an  z1 I've seen many people commenting that  Mellie Otis is now way too powerful and  there is no way that the demon king can  ever hope to defeat him we have to  remember that Mellie Otis can't just up  and kill the demon king because the  demon king is using sell Jess's body as  a vessel  so if meliodas chooses to kill him he  will also kill his own brother  we know meliodas hasn't been the best  big brother but i don't think he will go  as far as killing zell drous this means  that meliodas will be forced to hold  back and with the demon king being as  ruthless as he is and with the Endura  coming from the demon realm to help the  demon king it is likely that this fight  will be a very difficult one for  meliodas and the sins but if we think  about it rationally this makes sense it  wouldn't be much fun if millie oldest  was just able to destroy the demon king  easily all on his own and the fact that  we're seeing such heavy foreshadowing  about Arthur and Excalibur indicates  that Arthur probably will be needed in  order to help defeat the demon king or  maybe even some other threat down the  line such as the supreme deity it just  wouldn't make sense for us to have seen  that vision from Hawks mama about the  new king being born and Arthur and  Excalibur being shown to us and it  wouldn't make sense to give us this  whole section about the Lady of the lake  if Arthur wasn't going to play an  important role in the future and since  we know that in the past there was talk  about a seven deadly sins spin-off that  would feature King Arthur as the next  protagonist Arthur's somehow coming back  to life would make this spin-off or  sequel a real possibility now moving on  to the rest of the chapter as the demon  king faces off against meliodas  the demon king says that the environment  is enraged because it doesn't need to  demon kings in this world and here the  demon king is referring to all the  natural disasters that have been taking  place all over Britannia by saying that  this world doesn't need to demon kings  the demon king is acknowledging that  melioidosis power has grown to such an  extent that he can now be considered a  demon king in his own right this is an  important admission by the demon king  because now it is clear that he is not  about to underestimate meliodas and his  power as he has done in the past but  meliodas says that the demon king is  wrong the world doesn't need even one  demon king and all of this needless  death and suffering over thousands of  years  been caused by the demon Kings worthless  quarrel with the supreme deity this is  an interesting statement because we  still don't know what the cause of the  conflict between the demon king and the  supreme deity was but many have  speculated that perhaps the two were  once lovers but they had a falling-out  and this is what led to the bloody holy  wars between the goddess and demon clans  by meliodas calling their conflict are  worthless quarrel he may be suggesting  that this was a lover's quarrel that got  out of control after all love and  heartbreak are both very powerful  motivators Mele Otis's words are not  clear here so we can't know for sure but  let me know down in the comments what  you think was the cause of the quarrel  between the demon king and the supreme  deity do you think that they were lovers  or do you think that the cause of their  conflict was something else entirely  following Mele Otis's impassioned speech  the demon king just scoffs at the idea  that the death and suffering experienced  by so many during the holy war should  concern him in the least he says that  these lives are like a stone or a grain  of sand by the road these lives mean  nothing to him the demon king is so much  more powerful than these other creatures  that he considers them to be lesser  life-forms and completely insignificant  in the grand scheme of things like  insects or grains of sand Mele Otis  states that he used to think this way to  back when he was the leader of the ten  commandments but meeting Elizabeth  changed him and he now understands the  value of life and he can now sympathize  with the struggles and challenges that  every living being has to face as they  go about living their own lives thanks  to Elizabeth and all of his friends  meliodas has experienced love compassion  friendship and so many other emotions  that every living being experiences and  he says that he will throw all of the  feelings of everyone who suffered or  lost their lives because of the holy  wars right in the demon King's faced  with that the epic battle between demon  King's eldest and meliodas finally  begins the two overpowered titans begin  to exchange blows as the environment  goes crazy all around them in the final  panel of the chapter Mele Otis appears  to gain the upper hand as he lands a  solid punch on the demon King's face but  we all know that this punch will not be  the  after the recent events that we  witnessed in the manga and after all  that rolling by naka Basu tsuki we have  to pace ourselves and we can't jump to  any definitive conclusions my own  personal guess is that the fact that the  last two chapters directly referenced  Arthur and Arthurian legend is clear  foreshadowing that Arthur will return in  some capacity and I believe that Mellie  Otis and the others are going to need  his help in order to defeat the demon  king and perhaps eventually the supreme  deity  I predict that Arthur will return with a  huge power up and Mellie Otis and the  sins will work together with Arthur to  fully harness the power of the legendary  sword Excalibur and destroy the demon  king once and for all  then after that we may get the  announcement that an Arthur spin-off of  the seven deadly sins featuring Arthur  